{{ macros.section(3, "Call Forms", id="call-forms") }}

{% include "includes/callform-algebra.md" %}

The unified <a href="{{_}}/cmk/concepts/#callforms">call-form</a> grammar over three
<b>anchors</b>: <code>this.</code> (a target), <code>cmk.</code> (a macro/function), and the
anchorless <b>receiver</b> (a <code>declare.*</code> name).  Two flavors, combinable in either order:
argument-passing <code>(args)</code> and stream-passing <code>[stream]</code>.

<table class=quickref>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Call Form</th>
      <th>Syntax / Example</th>
      <th>Meaning</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><a href="{{_}}/cmk/metaprogramming/#dialects">Target &middot; bare</a></td>
      <td>{{ cmkmath.imath("`this.`@t") }}<br/><code>this.build</code></td>
      <td>Recursive make: <code>${make} </code><i>t</i>.  New subprocess, inherits the launch environment, triggers a reparse.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><a href="{{_}}/cmk/concepts/#callforms">Target &middot; args</a></td>
      <td>{{ cmkmath.imath("`this.`@t(@arg)") }}<br/><code>this.build(x)</code></td>
      <td>Pos-arg becomes the stem: <code>${make} </code><i>t</i><code>/</code><i>arg</i> (the <code>this.</code> anchor takes POS-ARGS only).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><a href="{{_}}/cmk/concepts/#callforms">Target &middot; stream</a></td>
      <td>{{ cmkmath.imath("`this.`@t[@stream]") }}<br/><code>this.eval[echo hi]</code></td>
      <td>Pipe stdin in: <i>stream</i><code> | ${make} </code><i>t</i>.  Stream may be a command, a literal, or a block-ref.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><a href="{{_}}/cmk/concepts/#callforms">Target &middot; tagged</a></td>
      <td><code>this.</code><i>t</i><code>'''…'''</code><br/><code>this.eval'''hi'''</code></td>
      <td>Tagged-string form: an ADJACENT triple-quote literal IS the <code>[stream]</code> (no brackets).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><a href="{{_}}/cmk/metaprogramming/#dialects">Macro &middot; args</a></td>
      <td>{{ cmkmath.imath("`cmk.`@fn(@args)") }}<br/><code>cmk.log(hi)</code></td>
      <td>Call a compose.mk function/macro: <code>$(call </code><i>fn</i><code>,</code><i>args</i><code>)</code>.  Comma-separated pos-args OR <code>key=val</code> kwargs.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><a href="{{_}}/cmk/concepts/#callforms">Macro &middot; stream</a></td>
      <td>{{ cmkmath.imath("`cmk.`@fn[@stream]") }}<br/><code>cmk.render(k=1)["""$$P"""]</code></td>
      <td><i>stream</i><code> | $(call </code><i>fn</i><code>,…)</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><a href="{{_}}/cmk/compiler/#receivers">Receiver</a></td>
      <td>{{ cmkmath.imath("@name.@method(@args)") }} &middot; {{ cmkmath.imath("[@stream]") }}<br/><code>inbox.emit["""hi"""]</code></td>
      <td>Anchorless send to a <code>declare.*</code> name (channel/module/polyglot/container): auto-<code>${make} </code><i>name</i><code>.</code><i>method</i>, no <code>this.</code> needed.  Fires only for a DECLARED name, at a word boundary, with a call-suffix.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><a href="{{_}}/cmk/metaprogramming/#about-dialects">Self</a></td>
      <td><code>__target__</code> &middot; <code>__target__[stream]</code><br/><code>__target__[echo hi]</code></td>
      <td>The running target as a callable (<code>this.__target_name__</code>): a recursive self-send, e.g. <code>… | ${make} ${@}</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><a href="{{_}}/cmk/concepts/#callforms">Combined (args + stream)</a></td>
      <td>{{ cmkmath.imath("@anchor.@name(@args)[@stream]") }}<br/><code>cmk.render(n=app)["""$$P"""]</code></td>
      <td>Arguments AND stdin together, for both <code>this.</code> and <code>cmk.</code>; either order (<code>(a)[s]</code> == <code>[s](a)</code>).</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

