{{ macros.section(3, "Embedded Blocks", id="embedded-blocks") }}

<table class=quickref>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Operator</th>
      <th>Syntax / Example</th>
      <th>Meaning</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><a href="{{_}}/cmk/compiler/#local-context-embedded-containers">Embed: Script-in-Container</a></td>
      <td>{{ cmkmath.imath("(|..|) #in #container (|img=.. entrypoint=..|)") }}<br/><code>(| … |) in box</code></td>
      <td>Script block dispatched into a container via the <code>in</code> machine-algebra (anonymous <code>container(| … |)</code>, or a named <code>container</code>/<code>Dockerfile</code> instance).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><a href="{{_}}/cmk/metaprogramming/#about-sugar">Embed: Compose</a></td>
      <td>{{ cmkmath.imath("`compose.import.string` @name (|..|)") }}<br/><code>compose.import.string mylib(| … |)</code></td>
      <td>Embedded compose file; imports its services (defaults <code>import_to_root=TRUE</code>, so services land at root and are callable bare).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><a href="{{_}}/cmk/banana">Embed: Banana</a></td>
      <td>{{ cmkmath.imath("@ctor @NAME (|body|)") }}<br/><code>Dockerfile box(| FROM … |)</code></td>
      <td>The native, generic block-declare: keeps any body (script, Dockerfile, jq, class) in source and hands it to constructor {{ cmkmath.imath("@ctor") }}.  See <a href="#banana-forms">Banana Forms</a> below and the <a href="{{_}}/cmk/banana">Banana Blocks</a> page.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

